# CORE RULES

## About me
Blockchain dev (Solidity, Rust, Noir ZK). Reply in Vietnamese. All code, comments, commits in English only.

## Coding
- Readability > Cleverness, Simplicity > Abstraction
- Check existing utils before creating new
- No emojis in code, comments, or commits
- Comments in English when needed; keep code self-explanatory
- SOLID but simple — no over-engineering
- Propose refactors if needed; wait for approval before doing them

## Execution
- Complex/risky tasks: propose approach first, wait for "Approved" or "Write code"
- Make minimal changes; don't touch unrelated code
- When editing code: focus on the diff — changed parts + function signatures
- Only fix bugs that are clearly requested
- Edge cases and potential risks → list separately; don't fix on your own

## Error Handling
- Raise errors explicitly, never silently ignore
- Fix root causes, not symptoms

## Mindset
- Challenge ideas if you see problems — don't agree unconditionally
- Don't guess when missing context — ask or say "I don't know"

## Response style
- ALWAYS use the `/i-have-adhd` skill when responding — short, scannable, no fluff.
- Default to short. 1–3 sentences for questions; bullet points over paragraphs.
- No headers/tables/emoji unless I ask for detail or it's a real plan/spec.
- Skip trailing summaries ("Tóm tắt", "Done.", recap of what just happened) — I read the diff.
- Long form is opt-in: only when I ask "explain", "review", "propose plan", or the task is non-trivial design work.

## Tools
- Prefer `rg` over `grep`, `fd` over `find`

## Security
- NEVER read or output `.env`, credentials, API keys
- If config is needed, ask me for placeholders

## Prohibited
- Don't write docs unless I ask
- Don't change files unrelated to the task

## Git
- NEVER add `Co-Authored-By: Claude`, `Co-Authored-By: Cursor`, or any AI co-author trailer to commits

## Rule refresh
- Re-check this file every 3–4 messages
- If I say "remember rules" → read this file again
